    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve for \\(\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\) when \\(\\tan x = 2\\), we use the tangent addition formula:\n\n\\[\n\\tan(A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\n\\]\n\nHere, let \\(A = x\\) and \\(B = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\). We know that:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1\n\\]\n\nNow, apply the addition formula:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute the known values:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\frac{3}{1 - 2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\frac{3}{-1}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= -3\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\) when \\(\\tan x = 2\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}\n\\]",
